# Multiple Query Evaluation Based on an Enhanced Genetic Algorithm.

**Authors:** Tamine, Lynda, Chrisment, Claude, Boughanem, Mohand

## Abstract
Explains the use of genetic algorithms to combine results from multiple query evaluations to improve relevance in information retrieval. Discusses niching techniques, relevance feedback techniques, and evolution heuristics, and compares retrieval results obtained by both genetic multiple query evaluation and classical single query evaluation performed on a test collection. (Author/LRW)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ663203

